# Every path, one owner. A ruleset on `main` requires a review from a code owner
# on every pull request, so this file is what makes "reviewed before it lands"
# mean something rather than being a setting nobody is named by.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the catch-all comes first and anything
# needing a different owner goes below it.
* @AymericP

# The three files that decide what the pipeline is allowed to do, and the one
# that decides what gets published. Listed separately not because the owner
# differs but because a diff here deserves reading twice: a change to a workflow
# or to the publishing configuration changes what runs with write access.
/.github/            @AymericP
/pyproject.toml      @AymericP
/uv.lock             @AymericP
